#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299758 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca3eaad9-1dc3-55cb-ab62-7139f24f233d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298432}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298432} :answer-field/id #uuid "fef19aba-acb5-5246-8048-25a4732b0153" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d6120ca6-9e08-5dd7-8756-664c0b14c937" :question/math-academy-id "q-319420" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n${a}_{31}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & =1\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\,(2+1)-0\\,(0-1)+2\\,(-0-2) \\\\  & =3-0-4 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}^{t}={c}_{13}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{13} & =(-1)^{1+3}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =+\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-0 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{31}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299761 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a25d310-05ab-55e4-a1c5-609bfd85c0b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297780}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297780} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a79b5b0-3b96-5509-bde8-4a7499f7d418" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298732}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b74699a3-68fd-5996-962f-7d078766e370" :question/math-academy-id "q-319434" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & k\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $\\frac{1}{3}$ and $det(A)=1-2k.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=1-2k\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(1\\cdot k-0\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1-2k)}\\cdot (-k) \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{\\,2k-1\\,}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=\\frac{1}{3}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{\\,2k-1\\,} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 3k & =2k-1 \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299762 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6821836-cff5-597c-bfe8-284e273211b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298473}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298473} :answer-field/id #uuid "5334a997-fbd8-5492-a178-58a2c8133561" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d4e42e14-a47f-5067-a3e2-ccca26a8935c" :question/math-academy-id "q-319437" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $\\frac{1}{2}$ and $det(A)=k-1.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=k-1\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}^{t}={c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(-1+2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-1}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{k-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{23}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{k-1} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ k-1 & =-2 \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299764 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19779c74-033c-527e-8527-75fcd9cd52be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9/2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297661}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297661} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a13f4b6-0d0b-5ddd-bc05-cb3e7f407353" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f7cdf079-0dbd-550b-985e-14ed1ec133fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-319442" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $\\frac{1}{4}$ and $det(A)=-2k-3.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=-2k-3\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}^{t}={c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(1+2) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2k-3)}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\,2k+3\\,}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{23}^{′}=\\frac{1}{4}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\,2k+3\\,} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 12 & =2k+3 \\\\ 2k & =9 \\\\ k & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299765 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9efe1417-3245-50a4-a08e-1226edd401f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2/3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298255}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298255} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2fd473d-2b44-5cd3-afbc-189ab115bc74" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299452}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "24df41a5-9c85-5f3d-b3b0-277ec8e095a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-319443" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & k & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $det(A)=k-2.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=k-2\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{13}^{t}={c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}\\begin{vmatrix}k & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}k & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =k+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(k-2)}\\cdot (k+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{k+2}{\\,k-2\\,}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{13}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k+2}{\\,k-2\\,} & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2(k+2) & =-(k-2) \\\\ 2k+4 & =-k+2 \\\\ 3k & =-2 \\\\ k & =-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299776 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67507fa1-9c8b-533b-b35f-b2b75970e742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297996}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297996} :answer-field/id #uuid "86f29c10-686e-51f4-8830-5217f4abdf63" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2b5cf762-3178-5e63-a1b0-8da0e65dccf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-319546" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nif its determinant is $17.$\n\n${a}_{13}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\,1\\cdot (1\\cdot 4-0\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\,{c}_{31} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{17}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299777 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30fc4049-b346-5ef3-b721-8b7b6804b08f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297759}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297759} :answer-field/id #uuid "83e9901e-f892-512e-a362-56ac30375949" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "66b7eb82-0c6f-5154-a5bd-434c9571ba55" :question/math-academy-id "q-319549" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nif its determinant is $3.$\n\n${a}_{21}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\,(1\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\,{c}_{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299778 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c573351-ee99-56f5-889f-894b79759197" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298090}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298090} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e78f910-eafd-5dde-95e7-840e8bbf0359" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298904}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "959ebdb0-727b-5193-9194-4f73c8f717da" :question/math-academy-id "q-319550" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nif its determinant is $-22.$\n\n${a}_{33}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{33}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{33} & =(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\,1\\cdot (2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{33}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\,{c}_{33} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-22}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299801 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f879e289-265f-50e1-93a8-bc1f3228e612" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298611}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298611} :answer-field/id #uuid "66a8d0a5-264a-526a-bf26-7c2ead18114a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298984}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "dc09a39f-9bc3-5b8d-97b8-ec01ec4b162d" :question/math-academy-id "q-319859" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ k & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nequals $-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ k & -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}=1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ k & 2\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ k & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\,(1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-1))-2\\,(0\\cdot 2-1\\cdot k)+(-1)\\,(0\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot k) \\\\  & =(2+1)-2\\,(-k)+(-1)\\,(-k) \\\\  & =3+2k+k \\\\  & =3k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-(4-1) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3k+3}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{3k+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{2}$, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-3}{3k+3} & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -3k-3 & =-6 \\\\ -3k & =-6+3 \\\\ k & =\\frac{-3}{-3} \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299809 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbeaf4d4-0e00-520e-99d0-3bee5b93deca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298438}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298438} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcfa3e0a-bb95-5124-94ff-faa0c2a5654f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7aba959b-00b2-5aea-a09a-80fa0c6d7e58" :question/math-academy-id "q-319937" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & k & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nequals $-1.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & k & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ k & -2\\end{vmatrix}-(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(1\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot k)+(0\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot 3)+(0\\cdot k-1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =2(k-2)+3-3 \\\\  & =2k-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}^{t}={c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(2\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-(-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{23}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2k-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{23}^{′}=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{k-2} & =-1 \\\\ 1 & =-(k-2) \\\\ k-2 & =-1 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299812 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00f85809-939f-5696-b20f-6a24d1b3a8b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297553}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297553} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c533b51-00bb-5918-948d-af70d14f79e3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "44f3f3e2-3340-514f-8bf3-b71afd4ac18e" :question/math-academy-id "q-319944" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ k & -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nequals $-2.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ k & -2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ k & -1\\end{vmatrix}+(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ k & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-2)((-1)(-1)-(-2)(-2))+2((-2)(-1)-(-2)k)+(-2)((-2)(-2)-(-1)k) \\\\  & =(-2)(1-4)+2(2+2k)+(-2)(4+k) \\\\  & =6+4+4k-8-2k \\\\  & =2k+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{32}^{t}={c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ k & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-((-2)(-2)-(-2)k) \\\\  & =-(4+2k) \\\\  & =-2k-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{32}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2k-4}{2k+2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{k+2}{k+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{32}^{′}=-2$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{k+2}{k+1} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{k+2}{k+1} & =2 \\\\ k+2 & =2k+2 \\\\ k & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bec7eef-98ab-50a1-a827-b84e71a0b5c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300251} {:answer/id #uuid "3f84bdbb-e043-5047-a36e-5da69a5c79e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300274} {:answer/id #uuid "48bd8464-99de-5369-8e7b-9fe677ea1700" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300331} {:answer/id #uuid "a04b15ad-a1bc-5b8c-b98c-a273e45d97d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300771} {:answer/id #uuid "a93e42c1-d25f-5c74-aa8c-ac931bf2b4fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300810}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300251} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf01f982-1095-5239-a807-cfb6858ba6e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301851}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f43456bf-f295-5e3b-a9b3-15b153a5e800" :question/math-academy-id "q-32727" :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle S=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & ={s}_{11}{C}_{11}+{s}_{12}{C}_{12}+{s}_{13}{C}_{13}+{s}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+2\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =2{C}_{12} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}2} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ 1 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & -5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(-1)^{1+2}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-2\\left(1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{vmatrix}\\right) \\\\  & =-2((-5\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 2)-0+0) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (-18) \\\\  & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302372 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0abde6ff-968f-5c10-a57e-e9337ccb9853" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-198" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299986} {:answer/id #uuid "0c0b0e8c-b5e8-5d1a-8a64-83154e74252f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299995} {:answer/id #uuid "1824105f-b810-5b30-a0aa-0beb57bd268f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-108" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300062} {:answer/id #uuid "6e3832ab-4326-5da4-9681-13c8424ca43e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300518} {:answer/id #uuid "b97de0dc-d8bc-5f26-9307-169bdbb2d021" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-432" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300890}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300890} :answer-field/id #uuid "54890664-57f3-5254-b119-6383b3902222" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301501}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8643e81c-8c77-5255-a120-2681f124c049" :question/math-academy-id "q-32791" :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle T=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 6 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & ={t}_{11}{C}_{11}+{t}_{12}{C}_{12}+{t}_{13}{C}_{13}+{t}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+4\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =-{C}_{11}+4{C}_{13} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}-1} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 6 & 0 & 2 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 0 & 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+4\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}4} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ 9 & 0 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 0 \\\\ -1 & 6 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+4\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}\\begin{vmatrix}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\left(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\\right)+4\\left(9\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}\\right) \\\\  & =-0+4\\cdot 9(6\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =36\\cdot (-12) \\\\  & =-432\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302373 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a74fc00-fd64-5b42-9d9b-22c961b3e9a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}7 & -3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 8 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -9 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300080} {:answer/id #uuid "456f14d2-c05d-5f77-a95f-02402a88764b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 8 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -9 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300308} {:answer/id #uuid "d80443ba-23ec-52cf-8364-fc8db3ddda93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 8 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -9 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301037} {:answer/id #uuid "e535d5d8-1a5b-50ea-bcd5-0d5de112cc6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 8 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 10\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301098} {:answer/id #uuid "ea6110fe-7888-57df-94d3-e8bd05499930" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 8 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 10\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301122}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301098} :answer-field/id #uuid "387a8cf8-7099-56dd-8883-b322ddd9523b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301410}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7ce9f7cf-7221-5005-8e3f-a5d9b8f1addd" :question/math-academy-id "q-32793" :question/problem "Find the cofactor of ${d}_{15}$ in \n$$\n\\displaystyle D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & -3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -9 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 10 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, to get the minor of ${d}_{15}$, we remove the $1$st row and $5$th column: \n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{gray}2}} \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 & 0 & {\\color{gray}∗} \\\\ 6 & 2 & -9 & 4 & {\\color{gray}∗} \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 1 & {\\color{gray}∗} \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 10 & {\\color{gray}∗}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n \nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{15}=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 8 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 10\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the cofactor of ${d}_{15}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{15} & =(-1)^{1+5}{M}_{15} \\\\  & ={M}_{15} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 8 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 10\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323744 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "147888b7-3be1-5c61-a527-09bd238c54f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321314} {:answer/id #uuid "57a12085-d4fa-57ec-8059-de705274f776" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321836} {:answer/id #uuid "8f51fed1-08a6-55a3-a261-1c9416d371f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322285} {:answer/id #uuid "ab001798-4c95-52c6-8bb5-a0283265953d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322489} {:answer/id #uuid "de5ed94a-712c-5cd7-b285-0cdfce1efa19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322884}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186322489} :answer-field/id #uuid "910c107e-8209-55ad-aaee-2dfef20df5ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323452}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9ae55842-6a04-591a-82b0-c1e71e70c4a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-36043" :question/problem "Find the cofactor of ${b}_{34}$ in \n$$\n\\displaystyle B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, to get the minor of ${b}_{34}$, we remove the $3$rd row and the $4$th column: \n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 3 & {\\color{gray}∗} \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & {\\color{gray}∗} \\\\ {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{gray}-2}} \\\\ -7 & 0 & 0 & {\\color{gray}∗}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{34}=\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the cofactor of ${b}_{34}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{34} & =(-1)^{3+4}{M}_{34} \\\\  & =-{M}_{34} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323745 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e995287-b0ce-5d14-adf9-a8c9c41bfbc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321381} {:answer/id #uuid "2135e8a8-7aa1-5be7-a729-d18fff9337df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-51" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321397} {:answer/id #uuid "23cebe08-003e-58dd-b604-3b895669fb51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321421} {:answer/id #uuid "30a88961-6b47-51d0-bc38-90b444ad5cdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-62" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321521} {:answer/id #uuid "ec560ecf-e9c3-5994-aee2-a1534c401d48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323004}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321521} :answer-field/id #uuid "9029e3eb-d47c-517f-8e68-1e0ac69f0975" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5505f107-cfef-57b0-b433-16953d2d1848" :question/math-academy-id "q-36045" :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle Z=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Z) & ={z}_{11}{C}_{11}+{z}_{12}{C}_{12}+{z}_{13}{C}_{13}+{z}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =1\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & ={C}_{11}-{C}_{13} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}1} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}∗} & -3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 4 & 3 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}-1} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ 0 & 0 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 5\\end{vmatrix}-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}5 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\\right)-\\left(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\\right) \\\\  & =0+2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+0-(0-0+0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2((-3)\\cdot 5-4\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-31) \\\\  & =-62\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323746 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c5244df-f0a9-5c2e-a73e-51aa0a825ac6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-178" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321614} {:answer/id #uuid "4c8e0c45-d2b6-5efa-8628-e01af954659c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "148" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321750} {:answer/id #uuid "52dec254-4e05-5958-b362-9315402fc410" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-371" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321800} {:answer/id #uuid "db1797e4-6de8-5d10-b3fb-c58f8e24e85f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "315" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322864} {:answer/id #uuid "f5e68f5c-b2e0-51fc-9ac1-cb001e6b3caa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "157" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323074}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321750} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f090c82-dafa-5202-866e-f37a38c4880e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "59bec8fd-d214-5893-9146-596b7aabe9e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-36053" :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle U=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & ={u}_{11}{C}_{11}+{u}_{12}{C}_{12}+{u}_{13}{C}_{13}+{u}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =5\\cdot {C}_{11}+(-2)\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =5{C}_{11}-2{C}_{12} \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}5} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 6 & 0 & 1 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 2 & 5 & -4\\end{vmatrix}+(-2)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}-2} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ 0 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 5 & -4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & -4\\end{vmatrix}+(-2)\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =5\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & -4\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =5\\left(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{vmatrix}-1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}\\right)+2\\left(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{vmatrix}-1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{vmatrix}\\right) \\\\  & =5(0-(6\\cdot (-4)-1\\cdot 2)+0)+2(0-(3\\cdot (-4)-1\\cdot (-3))+0) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 26+2\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =130+18 \\\\  & =148\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326843 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07f00af2-b840-5786-b28b-1f6973830285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324045} {:answer/id #uuid "b0650f26-5533-5b0a-9347-28807009e5c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325475} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e20584-c42b-540c-abb4-0d75908bf38f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325812} {:answer/id #uuid "e0878097-34b5-589b-a86b-0981c9097b18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325933} {:answer/id #uuid "fde0d5e3-6d10-584d-a825-0b58e5e1d31b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-5 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326210}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324045} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec36ae3f-3647-5b17-9422-159a73ac8d97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326646}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ed7ec0b2-f754-51c2-b65a-169d7f4dad10" :question/math-academy-id "q-40449" :question/problem "Find the cofactor of ${a}_{13}$ in \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -2 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, to get the minor of ${a}_{13}$,  we remove the $1$st row and the $3$rd column:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{gray}1}} & {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} \\\\ 0 & 2 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 7 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -5 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 1 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{13}=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the cofactor of ${a}_{13}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{13} & =(-1)^{1+3}{M}_{13} \\\\  & ={M}_{13} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338990 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13874c69-ce11-5c4a-b0db-84ef83ade9dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336218} {:answer/id #uuid "5e1b6947-b6e0-5826-8441-dbb3d0b931fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336883} {:answer/id #uuid "a2c180a6-138d-5a7f-9d31-a404b45cc073" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337510} {:answer/id #uuid "ece790d0-e97b-5afe-a665-0bd073ac46d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338100} {:answer/id #uuid "fa94f849-7016-5d56-965c-7206ff571a1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338230}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338230} :answer-field/id #uuid "19deb739-c9c7-5b2d-8ffb-a8a00f607b7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9f3afffa-5f2d-5a4d-8c50-83d3e9705709" :question/math-academy-id "q-71800" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y &=7 \\\\ x+y &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation, all the variables are on the left-hand side, and all the constants are on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y &=7 \\\\ x+y &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338992 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "092149d4-4746-597d-b469-fd9e124145a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336110} {:answer/id #uuid "0a6aba9a-03cf-5963-9982-db4dd212466f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336129} {:answer/id #uuid "734fe104-fc87-5937-ab79-b8a96359e482" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337072} {:answer/id #uuid "d0c39530-814f-58b1-87ba-a2ce667a5978" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337859} {:answer/id #uuid "ff0d859f-843c-5762-8a71-9acb0d107736" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338271}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336110} :answer-field/id #uuid "77ca8a8e-7cde-5776-a055-3d15385c87dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6fb63d0f-068a-51bd-a44a-a1afcc574af8" :question/math-academy-id "q-71804" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+5y &=-1 \\\\ 5x &=15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. \nThe variable $y$ does not appear in the second equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+5y &=-1 \\\\ 5x+0y &=15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339016 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fd7bbbf-6e0c-51c5-a9fa-fc0f2bf1d945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467896} {:answer/id #uuid "c58e8001-ca94-52dc-9ac3-efcb68b4cfa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467897}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467897} :answer-field/id #uuid "0afb67d1-8168-5df5-930f-8190b07edc62" :answer-field/key "$R=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468669} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6fa4bf8-f217-5274-8dab-28c162bb278d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467898} {:answer/id #uuid "f93fd016-1442-53ad-8597-12bc1e59568b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467899}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467899} :answer-field/id #uuid "a00bd3e1-111e-5780-871b-467da013e81a" :answer-field/key "$S=\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468670} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f78fc2c-5319-559a-b65c-0b1064d9bbc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467900} {:answer/id #uuid "906cb48c-7d29-5136-a248-2c29457a1fee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467901}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467900} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4c5cafc-4559-5564-a3f4-1bb51c7edb62" :answer-field/key "$T=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6118feb2-c751-599a-b3b9-c8c760c49b6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-71934" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $R$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(R)=5\\cdot 4-10\\cdot 2=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(R)=0,$ we conclude that $R$ is not invertible.\n\n- The matrix $S$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $T$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(T)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $T$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $R$ and $S$ do not have an inverse."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339017 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b04e9358-9109-5802-a83d-c003136f6776" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467902} {:answer/id #uuid "711d5a0b-0232-5cb7-8a88-a13f69141094" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467903}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467903} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b39826b-4d43-597b-b35d-5dd3a91ceaf8" :answer-field/key "$X=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 6 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468672} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af6e952f-1b3d-5415-9986-1f855a35a9dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467904} {:answer/id #uuid "d5a6c71b-66a8-52d7-88ab-87e3a0607923" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467905}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467904} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f838e05-1a03-57ee-8f9c-10a9e960bcdd" :answer-field/key "$Y=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468673} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e98450e-f707-5f45-880a-72823035ac85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467906} {:answer/id #uuid "3b62048c-e540-5983-8cbf-aabcf18ff59a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467907}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467906} :answer-field/id #uuid "2386ffd6-0069-5a17-ae65-0bf5f760c977" :answer-field/key "$Z=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f09c20fa-fbe3-5a9f-8218-d2a4dd2af13c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71938" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $X$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Y$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Y)=6\\cdot 6-7\\cdot 5=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Y)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Y$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Z$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Z)=(-2)\\cdot 5-10\\cdot 1=-20.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Z)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Z$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $X$ does not have an inverse."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339028 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16f0d1eb-63da-516d-b39c-98936ea702c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336248} {:answer/id #uuid "3e475449-d5a0-5355-9040-0c60f6ed7506" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336619} {:answer/id #uuid "4b8e773e-5ecc-5ed1-a6ae-65cce087450b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336734} {:answer/id #uuid "94bf4718-c6d0-59d1-9ec4-b22670dd22eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337391} {:answer/id #uuid "96bb9ff0-d964-5085-8a7c-e0e55abb0c09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337403}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337403} :answer-field/id #uuid "01585e92-cf9f-5695-8971-52db4143edc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1f42b909-72e3-5c68-a789-fc35f80e300c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71967" :question/problem "If $V=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & y \\\\ 5 & y\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $V$ is singular if and only if $det(V)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(V) & =7\\cdot y-5\\cdot y \\\\  & =7y-5y \\\\  & =2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y & =0 \\\\ y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $y$ is $y=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339029 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1608f206-6cae-571f-8d1e-16b6d162d46d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=\\pm 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336238} {:answer/id #uuid "287ca0dc-331e-527d-b8c0-e766a590d0c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=\\pm 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336411} {:answer/id #uuid "8f1fd271-6941-56e0-8167-86c17416a68a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337323} {:answer/id #uuid "9f6e027a-7384-58dc-b2bb-94433e7f22eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337473} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f32404-27a9-5015-979f-c6987e1fe3c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338010}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336411} :answer-field/id #uuid "53c72237-b3c8-5418-adbd-d5b4558f878e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d71eb817-7b8e-5d55-9dca-4bfa26de23cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-71968" :question/problem "If $H=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & c \\\\ c & 5\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $H$ is singular if and only if $det(H)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(H) & =5\\cdot 5-c\\cdot c \\\\  & =25-{c}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25-{c}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =25 \\\\ c & =\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $c$ are $c=\\pm 5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339030 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f062ffd-0731-5c9d-b5df-1e280483ad62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336623} {:answer/id #uuid "87e8b87b-9219-5612-bc47-0727af4eb0b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337259} {:answer/id #uuid "9d1a9b12-eb65-52f2-be17-471977096571" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337454} {:answer/id #uuid "db1521d6-6365-5c27-8635-662375c34db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337942} {:answer/id #uuid "e0112779-824d-50fa-a23d-b42b80a0e397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337989}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337259} :answer-field/id #uuid "82b667e3-83f0-533b-abd1-94355475f197" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338510}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "35c7dc25-96f0-5d9f-9d6a-dfbf5fcfb320" :question/math-academy-id "q-71969" :question/problem "If $M=\\begin{bmatrix}t & 4 \\\\ t & 10\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $M$ is singular if and only if $det(M)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =t\\cdot 10-t\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =10t-4t \\\\  & =6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6t & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $t$ is $t=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342006 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "444cd60d-98f8-57c7-9875-93fe9bccf0fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339729} {:answer/id #uuid "534e79d6-1a48-52d9-8361-6b5e12a9cdf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339897} {:answer/id #uuid "53b60466-c23f-5e4c-9676-8a33e27c13b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339902} {:answer/id #uuid "87d00cf2-3923-56f4-a41d-5b87aa3fb375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340345} {:answer/id #uuid "da2aff30-bbeb-5d42-9525-3fe5517ebd88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341064}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341064} :answer-field/id #uuid "45ff8668-6658-5885-8426-f8efdc154b15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341502}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4a069e33-ab79-5e52-8347-ee8dc3251c92" :question/math-academy-id "q-73535" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & k \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $\\frac{1}{4}$ and $det(A)=6+3k.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=6+3k\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{33}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{33} & =(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2-(-1) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{33}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{33} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6+3k}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2+k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{33}^{′}=\\frac{1}{4}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4} & =\\frac{1}{2+k} \\\\ 2+k & =4 \\\\ k & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342008 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "665c812a-56dd-5bc5-b0c8-ffde25e8fa1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340028} {:answer/id #uuid "ae5fface-39c3-5bf8-a1ce-22c8363e23e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340717} {:answer/id #uuid "b15c3399-c900-542c-998e-a75077eccf14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340742} {:answer/id #uuid "c27c70d1-a640-5ece-ae8a-27b55a8741af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340859} {:answer/id #uuid "e7fa4eea-3361-5d16-9459-3c3594fb683d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341175}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340028} :answer-field/id #uuid "2aa240fd-e96d-535e-8b4a-f32a7de1ce5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "33a7f588-04f8-5fc0-9705-3e73eb1453a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-73542" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ k & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $1.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ k & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}k & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\begin{vmatrix}k & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-2-0)+(-2k-0)+0 \\\\  & =-2k-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(1-(-3)) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2k-2}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{k+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{32}^{′}=1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{k+1} & =1 \\\\ 2 & =k+1 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342009 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05beee91-a392-5f65-88d2-f7fc95e409b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339177} {:answer/id #uuid "817291a6-cca7-53a6-bdbd-a95cc30beb48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340293} {:answer/id #uuid "98547d62-efa4-543b-b561-835c71d9986d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340498} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1fa043-012b-58dc-8eb3-9d118befac20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340804} {:answer/id #uuid "e51c2424-ac45-594a-b4be-5f0fea419df3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341155}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341155} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c974da0-7d8a-5c4f-9610-badc09e2e785" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341544}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "93b0be09-4ca6-5085-9855-e90445a7accc" :question/math-academy-id "q-73545" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{11}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & k\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $\\frac{4}{5}.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & k\\end{vmatrix} & =2\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix}+0\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(-k-6)-(0-3) \\\\  & =-2k-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{11}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{11}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{11} & =(-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-k-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{11} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2k-9}\\cdot (-k-6) \\\\  & =\\frac{k+6}{2k+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{11}^{′}=\\frac{4}{5}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k+6}{2k+9} & =\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ 5(k+6) & =4(2k+9) \\\\ 5k+30 & =8k+36 \\\\ 3k & =-6 \\\\ k & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348176 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b8bcb10-ac3e-55b6-b031-7dbf74e239f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345737} {:answer/id #uuid "59fd8952-62da-5a67-b9f7-07fe0e852847" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346119} {:answer/id #uuid "d49fb2b3-f414-5e50-a37a-0e6179c2bd77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347218} {:answer/id #uuid "ed42e7fe-6e5f-52f5-bd0b-40cd218c7c42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 8 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347444} {:answer/id #uuid "f42a5c98-7204-58b2-97fa-48ee5b75bef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347516}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347218} :answer-field/id #uuid "259e0501-a96f-5581-b7ba-bcbbab78467e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d05fea71-6716-5388-8215-29b86b42d217" :question/math-academy-id "q-7921" :question/problem "Calculate ${E}^{-1}$, where\n$$\n\\displaystyle E=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $E$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(E)}\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(E)=4\\cdot 7-8\\cdot 3=4\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(E)}\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E{E}^{-1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,{\\color{green}✓} \\\\ {E}^{-1}E & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,{\\color{green}✓}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348182 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20dd891b-d694-5499-8817-937a44eceff4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468238} {:answer/id #uuid "d5955946-ccfb-5755-8612-e0cdabb5eab7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468239}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468238} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a54a548-43f3-5af9-bb27-c37157e1ba17" :answer-field/key "$D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468840} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91fda060-34cb-56bf-a286-798cf5974bde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468240} {:answer/id #uuid "691d2f9b-6944-52d3-b95e-6577e5ed9262" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468241}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468241} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1dfcd78-f8c3-5201-b805-25717f44d7c0" :answer-field/key "$F=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468841} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44aed856-5960-53b9-88e1-18229b5f5d72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468242} {:answer/id #uuid "cbda35bc-2510-530d-8b17-8fd2a72ea3be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468243}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468242} :answer-field/id #uuid "121ad5e6-2d71-5c46-b7a0-42914d3db890" :answer-field/key "$G=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6cd97c58-6193-5fe7-8948-41d6f4bfcd71" :question/math-academy-id "q-7923" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $D$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(D)=3\\cdot 6-6\\cdot 2=6.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(D)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $D$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $F$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(F)=6\\cdot 6-6\\cdot 6=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(F)=0,$ we conclude that $F$ is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $G$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(G)=(-2)\\cdot 4-4\\cdot 2=-16.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(G)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $G$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $F$ does not have an inverse."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354631 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54be5f09-3b58-5930-bdc7-ccdb2f67d6da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352318} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca99045-dd33-5f43-a7c8-c5f10727365c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352525} {:answer/id #uuid "8711bd28-d757-5733-8d8e-74aa8e1eeb4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352748} {:answer/id #uuid "87cd6a64-8926-5898-b3a1-08617a82941b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352758} {:answer/id #uuid "dfede72a-5a0f-52ab-9653-3586280ead39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353513}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352748} :answer-field/id #uuid "27886f52-60bd-58ac-8062-d0a079292caa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353878}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "302f133a-6090-5037-99fd-6973d6637f17" :question/math-academy-id "q-8820" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y &=1 \\\\ x-8y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation, all the variables are on the left-hand side, and all the constants are on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y &=1 \\\\ x-8y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362383 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "742aed52-3923-5d3e-aae7-5ca575086d97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -10 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361349} {:answer/id #uuid "8ad587c3-4f5c-5eca-b96d-64e234660df7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361450} {:answer/id #uuid "a4c8cb0e-1acd-5b83-85e0-b9b1a7bde4b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361575} {:answer/id #uuid "caa1fb09-e645-5bb3-bc36-d3b843dcd6d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 9 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361752} {:answer/id #uuid "e206a94e-4884-53b0-b2c6-1a2394ba3c14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -10 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361847}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186361575} :answer-field/id #uuid "240210d3-d2e3-5a83-9c97-d93c03a1d0de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362012}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7e033a7c-c230-5700-a5b4-d8c955024d86" :question/math-academy-id "q-9967" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & =4\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4(-12+10)+2(32-35)+3(-16+21) \\\\  & =-8-6+15 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362389 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bfe9eb7-0858-52db-9dfb-831c6cfdd93e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361032} {:answer/id #uuid "92da08bc-b94a-5969-b999-e830f9be45bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361489} {:answer/id #uuid "d820da19-1020-5cd4-ad52-3b72b70b868e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361798} {:answer/id #uuid "dda5046b-7496-5105-85c6-0e609a2a6b0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361825} {:answer/id #uuid "e3499b31-131f-5fed-9b53-def82bb10a5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361854}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186361854} :answer-field/id #uuid "7631dea4-74c6-5439-9236-5c814d4472e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3e095599-c87c-5424-992d-faffcd2cd697" :question/math-academy-id "q-9980" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $\\frac{2}{5}.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & =2\\begin{vmatrix}k & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-3\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}4 & k \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(k-2)-3(4-6)+1(4-3k) \\\\  & =2k-4+6+4-3k \\\\  & =6-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(4-6) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-k}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{6-k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{21}^{′}=\\frac{2}{5}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{6-k} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 2\\cdot 5 & =2(6-k) \\\\ 10 & =12-2k \\\\ 2k & =2 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362402 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "360fced2-8218-5819-b49f-a6bdb1fc1bee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361080} {:answer/id #uuid "9c5a24fa-708c-583a-a345-c52f3aa911d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361533} {:answer/id #uuid "b26d0910-a34a-5209-9a33-b42495f6695f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361628} {:answer/id #uuid "c9642213-619d-5f39-b7b7-a194e5db904f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361747} {:answer/id #uuid "e3588d61-9553-531b-9d36-cee636d25f26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361855}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186361855} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ec73497-ac99-5d21-88bb-baefe07c1bbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361992}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "90452d65-c7b3-548e-83d9-2c700d6e9c0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-9998" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ k & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $-1.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ k & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & =0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}k & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}k & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0-2(2k-0)+2(k-0) \\\\  & =-4k+2k \\\\  & =-2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(4-2) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2k}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{k} & =-1 \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364112 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75cb1d88-be8f-565a-8892-48a303e64be2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 11 & 0 & -9 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364114} {:answer/id #uuid "e8e4de03-83b4-5eb7-85e7-5082d3d5faf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 11 & 3 & -9 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364115} {:answer/id #uuid "18a26160-0ecc-5cb6-a8e9-2502d70ef054" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & -9\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364116} {:answer/id #uuid "14b9fa6f-497e-5ef2-9a76-8cd1a476c61b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -8 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364117} {:answer/id #uuid "192fe4e1-90f7-57bb-9824-063dbac2dd60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -8 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364118}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364117} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3453afe-00bf-5199-ac64-1a8b6d15168a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364113}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e657c376-dc40-5550-9d65-c80b82ab3edb" :question/math-academy-id "q-36048" :question/problem "Find the cofactor of ${d}_{34}$ in \n$$\n\\displaystyle D=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -8 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & -9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, to get the minor of ${d}_{34}$, we remove the $3$rd row and $4$th column: \n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -8 & 2 & {\\color{gray}∗} & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 1 \\\\ {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{gray}6}} & {\\color{gray}∗} \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{34}=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -8 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the cofactor of ${d}_{34}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{34} & =(-1)^{3+4}{M}_{34} \\\\  & =-{M}_{34} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -8 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367324 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30ef06e0-089b-54f0-a23e-7a535dcf88b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 6 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 15 & -1 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 3 & 8\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367326} {:answer/id #uuid "f496b802-659a-5791-ba99-e764c38849f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 15 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 18 & 0 & -9 & -3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367327} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb96cad-f716-53b8-bb74-5986ffa26c47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 0 & 9 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -9 & -3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367328} {:answer/id #uuid "b7c4ed2f-07cf-5a5b-b00a-1257fb62002f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 0 & 9 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -9 & -3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367329} {:answer/id #uuid "811d9bf0-4181-5fb3-b9bc-1a817d08f88c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 6 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 15 & -1 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 3 & 8\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367330}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367326} :answer-field/id #uuid "301d66c1-40cb-5a16-aa7b-6dd3d5ee7b42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a9350630-2246-5e07-9684-2d3afcf4dc67" :question/math-academy-id "q-130908" :question/problem "Find the cofactor of ${q}_{55}$ in \n$$\n\\displaystyle Q=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 6 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 15 & -1 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 3 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 18 & 3 & 0 & -9 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, to get the minor of ${q}_{55}$, we remove the $5$th row and $5$th column: \n\n$$\nQ=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 6 & 2 & 0 & {\\color{gray}∗} \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 9 & {\\color{gray}∗} \\\\ 15 & -1 & -5 & 6 & {\\color{gray}∗} \\\\ 4 & -4 & 3 & 8 & {\\color{gray}∗} \\\\ {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{gray}-3}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{55}=\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 6 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 15 & -1 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 3 & 8\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the cofactor of ${q}_{55}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{55} & =(-1)^{5+5}{M}_{55} \\\\  & ={M}_{55} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 6 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 15 & -1 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 3 & 8\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368489 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b24999b4-78f0-5329-99e0-9ca8ec99e96d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368491} {:answer/id #uuid "c6b405a1-f147-50d8-b262-948b3ef91fbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368492} {:answer/id #uuid "bab4f45e-f87e-5831-ab73-67f9596249aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368493} {:answer/id #uuid "56b7a0be-62e3-5f15-890c-3f566007ac87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368494} {:answer/id #uuid "09276c8d-ed02-5de7-8af1-90fbb6f4aaae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368495}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368494} :answer-field/id #uuid "5366cce4-b95c-579d-bf5b-43c029e52ab3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "55021539-024c-5816-9b9c-0adaf5b9e403" :question/math-academy-id "q-36049" :question/problem "Find the cofactor of ${c}_{21}$ in  $C=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we get the minor corresponding to ${c}_{21}$, removing the $2$nd row and the $1$st column:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}∗} & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{gray}1}} & {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} \\\\ {\\color{gray}∗} & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ {\\color{gray}∗} & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{21}=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the cofactor of ${c}_{21}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}{M}_{21} \\\\  & =-{M}_{21} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368541 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea4df699-7d9c-5d0f-9c99-1f7c51c9eb05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368543} {:answer/id #uuid "d5501494-bc71-5997-8259-0e5ae5acb0ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368544} {:answer/id #uuid "6c10f6a2-fd34-5592-aac4-362e161f9a0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368545} {:answer/id #uuid "93b023b1-7456-560d-a37c-931aaca0765c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368546} {:answer/id #uuid "db2b9044-1bff-57ee-ae25-64a27083c912" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368547}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368543} :answer-field/id #uuid "db95a348-0986-5700-b656-e8563530f38a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368542}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "46279f1d-0462-5a35-b644-65d4c737b0e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-40212" :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle H=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(H) & ={h}_{11}{C}_{11}+{h}_{12}{C}_{12}+{h}_{13}{C}_{13}+{h}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {C}_{11}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{13} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}2} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 0 & 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}-1} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ 7 & 0 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 0 \\\\ -1 & 5 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\left(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\\right)-\\left(7\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}\\right) \\\\  & =2(0)-(7(-10)) \\\\  & =-(-70) \\\\  & =70\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382256 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5a77823-c6b0-5dfd-b080-ffe4cfc11f5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382258} {:answer/id #uuid "a381d779-2e85-5aaf-8b89-c41349f150fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382259} {:answer/id #uuid "3cb7cd1d-1fab-5c3b-9461-a541a4c58031" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382260} {:answer/id #uuid "f9757233-a669-5535-91c9-3301d2cdc860" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382261} {:answer/id #uuid "af3bcfe1-d593-5fe7-88cf-00c2b3af0a03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382262}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382261} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf58cd3e-d1ca-5107-be49-843e76215f44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382257}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "53b328c9-6698-53f6-9c7d-d6d44c5e77f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-73533" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $\\frac{1}{18}$ and $det(A)=-18.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=-18\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ k & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ k & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}\\cdot (2+k).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{13}^{′}=\\frac{1}{18}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{18}(2+k) & =\\frac{1}{18} \\\\ 2+k & =-1 \\\\ k & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386055 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e5a90ce-5f43-5f35-b7b8-583244a42439" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386057} {:answer/id #uuid "8602540d-4801-5042-9916-98e607f58c64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386058} {:answer/id #uuid "c57393fc-dedc-5a9b-9994-032d00d28eef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386059} {:answer/id #uuid "8bc9fb87-d9dc-5a6b-ab93-485448959e7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386060} {:answer/id #uuid "66812ddb-563d-5415-bd8f-27772bb7e151" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386061}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386060} :answer-field/id #uuid "e416161a-9bd1-5b5b-810d-ebf9a09026af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "852dcdfe-ad8b-55fc-ab02-b3cb773c55c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-103533" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A)=4.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388174 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ac94783-3833-5c62-b8ff-99e49318afa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}8 & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388176} {:answer/id #uuid "c9e5b38f-c2e8-543b-b00d-cd4bd8f73e6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ -7 & 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388177} {:answer/id #uuid "9b8b2ac7-7ee9-5860-8395-e3dfed4ac549" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 8 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3 & 3 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388178} {:answer/id #uuid "89206cee-d78a-5591-9695-a660fc57e756" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 19 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388179} {:answer/id #uuid "aa54b09e-b6a0-545e-bd70-1a19ce8da4bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 19 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ -7 & 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388180}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388177} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd894676-d9a2-51c4-b3ed-225d4bfba13d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "27064447-2648-5562-9eb6-77f50dae0ce5" :question/math-academy-id "q-130822" :question/problem "What is the minor of ${q}_{22}$ in \n$$\n\\displaystyle Q=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 8 & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 19 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 8 \\\\ -7 & 4 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get the minor of ${q}_{22}$, we remove the $2$nd row and $2$nd column:\n\n$$\nQ=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & {\\color{gray}∗} & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ {\\color{gray}∗} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} & {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} \\\\ 0 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 0 & 8 \\\\ -7 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{22}=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ -7 & 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388188 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32af6844-5246-5136-9000-3ee064ffc19f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 11 & 0 & -9 & 11\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388190} {:answer/id #uuid "d737f210-dea9-5f09-a66e-aa69dee797b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{5} & 3 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & 11\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388191} {:answer/id #uuid "b8de215d-f356-52db-9dfe-292de5b13226" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{5} & 3 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & 11\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388192} {:answer/id #uuid "792dcc1e-8af6-5018-a2ca-9221df1a6e4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{5} & 8 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & 11\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388193} {:answer/id #uuid "1840b511-aeb2-52cf-bd75-d8d4779c7441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 11 & 0 & -9 & 11\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388194}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388190} :answer-field/id #uuid "f16b4332-934a-537a-8f1f-9d31b9413455" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388189}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2ead9650-2d18-5f36-b35f-cc2f4e8392b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-130905" :question/problem "Find the cofactor of ${g}_{42}$ in \n$$\n\\displaystyle G=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -2 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{5} & 3 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & -9 & 11\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, to get the minor of ${g}_{42}$, we remove the $4$th row and $2$nd column: \n\n$$\nG=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -2 \\\\ 3 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 0 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 0 & {\\color{gray}∗} & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ {\\color{gray}∗} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{gray}\\sqrt{5}}} & {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} \\\\ 11 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 0 & -9 & 11\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{42}=\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 11 & 0 & -9 & 11\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the cofactor of ${g}_{42}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{42} & =(-1)^{4+2}{M}_{42} \\\\  & ={M}_{42} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 11 & 0 & -9 & 11\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390791 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f17fc7e8-0774-59d5-a669-3e615ebed902" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 8 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 11 & 2\\end{vmatrix}" 